{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-tags-page-tsx","path":"/blog/tags/talks/","result":{"data":{"tags":{"group":[{"fieldValue":"fuzzing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"linux","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"papers","totalCount":5},{"fieldValue":"pharos","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"programming","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"prolog","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"publications","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"research","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"reverse engineering","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"skiing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"talks","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"travel","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"web","totalCount":2}]},"posts":{"totalCount":2,"edges":[{"node":{"html":"<p>My family and I had quite the day attending the <a href=\"https://www.cposc.org\">2023 Central Pennsylvania Open\nSource Conference (CPOSC)</a> yesterday at the Ware Center\nin Lancaster, PA.  In addition to attending, we spoke in three different talks!</p>\n<p>My wife, Dr. Stephanie Schwartz, kicked things off.  <figure class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figure\" style=\"\">\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/f13a9/steph.avif 200w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/af71e/steph.avif 400w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/c9875/steph.avif 800w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/07e28/steph.avif 1200w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/2babf/steph.avif 1600w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/95b77/steph.avif 2048w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/ba381/steph.webp 200w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/7f61c/steph.webp 400w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/d00b9/steph.webp 800w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/92f8c/steph.webp 1200w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/fad48/steph.webp 1600w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/8df42/steph.webp 2048w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/e07e9/steph.jpg 200w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/066f9/steph.jpg 400w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/4b190/steph.jpg 800w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/e5166/steph.jpg 1200w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/b17f8/steph.jpg 1600w,\n/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/e1596/steph.jpg 2048w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n            type=\"image/jpeg\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/5e403f4ebefe3b13be78183c9d16f8f1/4b190/steph.jpg\"\n            alt=\"Stephanie\npresenting\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n    </span>\n    <figcaption class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figcaption\">Stephanie\npresenting</figcaption>\n  </figure>  She gave a short introduction on Random Forests as an\nintroduction for her student Samantha Noggle, in \"Machine Learning Techniques to\nImprove Users' Music Listening Experiences\".  I thought Samantha did a great job\non her presentation.  It was an interesting topic that she presented at just the\nright level of detail.</p>\n<p>Next, my step son Nick Elzer, along with his coworker from\n<a href=\"https://www.quub.space\">Quub</a>, Nathaniel Every, gave his first ever public\nconference presentation, and did a great job!  <figure class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figure\" style=\"\">\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/f13a9/nick.avif 200w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/af71e/nick.avif 400w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/c9875/nick.avif 800w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/07e28/nick.avif 1200w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/2babf/nick.avif 1600w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/95b77/nick.avif 2048w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/ba381/nick.webp 200w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/7f61c/nick.webp 400w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/d00b9/nick.webp 800w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/92f8c/nick.webp 1200w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/fad48/nick.webp 1600w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/8df42/nick.webp 2048w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/e07e9/nick.jpg 200w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/066f9/nick.jpg 400w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/4b190/nick.jpg 800w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/e5166/nick.jpg 1200w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/b17f8/nick.jpg 1600w,\n/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/e1596/nick.jpg 2048w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n            type=\"image/jpeg\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/dfdfd2ba33babbf1d62c4d7acd43c816/4b190/nick.jpg\"\n            alt=\"Nick and Nathaniel\npresenting\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n    </span>\n    <figcaption class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figcaption\">Nick and Nathaniel\npresenting</figcaption>\n  </figure>  Their presentation was \"SpaceHeX Beta1.0 Release - What\nIf, For Space Hardware Development, We Put Each Egg In Its Own Basket?\", and was\nabout SpaceHex, a prototyping system they open sourced to make it easier for\npeople to break into satellite development.  They also demoed a pretty sweet\nomnidirectional rover that they built (at 2am the night before, naturally).</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet\"><p lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Started the open source repo for our space hardware development platform <a href=\"https://t.co/cRzHZkM6Gg\">https://t.co/cRzHZkM6Gg</a><br><br>Had a blast presenting with <a href=\"https://twitter.com/Nick_elzer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@Nick_elzer</a> for <a href=\"https://twitter.com/quubspace?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@quubspace</a>!<br><br>Thank you <a href=\"https://twitter.com/CPOSC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">@CPOSC</a> for having us! <a href=\"https://t.co/eRoHm5ea2u\">pic.twitter.com/eRoHm5ea2u</a></p>&mdash; Nathaniel Evry (@NathanielEvry) <a href=\"https://twitter.com/NathanielEvry/status/1642204542921064452?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">April 1, 2023</a></blockquote> <script async src=\"https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js\" charset=\"utf-8\"></script>\n<p>Finally, I gave a tutorial presentation called \"Introduction to Exploiting Stack\nBuffer Overflow Vulnerabilities\".  If you want, you can follow along\n<a href=\"https://github.com/edmcman/cposc-exploit\">here</a>. <figure class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figure\" style=\"\">\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/f13a9/ed.avif 200w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/af71e/ed.avif 400w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/c9875/ed.avif 800w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/07e28/ed.avif 1200w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/2babf/ed.avif 1600w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/95b77/ed.avif 2048w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/ba381/ed.webp 200w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/7f61c/ed.webp 400w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/d00b9/ed.webp 800w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/92f8c/ed.webp 1200w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/fad48/ed.webp 1600w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/8df42/ed.webp 2048w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/e07e9/ed.jpg 200w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/066f9/ed.jpg 400w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/4b190/ed.jpg 800w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/e5166/ed.jpg 1200w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/b17f8/ed.jpg 1600w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/e1596/ed.jpg 2048w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"\n            type=\"image/jpeg\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/4b190/ed.jpg\"\n            alt=\"Me speaking\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n    </span>\n    <figcaption class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figcaption\">Me speaking</figcaption>\n  </figure>  In\ntheory, there are supposed to be videos of all three talks eventually.  I'll\npost them when they are made available.</p>\n<p>After a few years of hiatus, it was great to have CPOSC 2023 be back in person\nagain.  I saw a number of great presentations, and met a lot of interesting and\nsmart people.  It's always surprising how many technical people work in an area\nthat is known for its rural farming!</p>","timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2023-04-02--cposc-2023/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["talks"],"title":"CPOSC 2023","updatedDate":"02 April, 2023","image":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/1400e/ed.jpg","srcSet":"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/1400e/ed.jpg 700w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/8ea22/ed.jpg 1400w","sizes":"700px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/a7167/ed.webp 700w,\n/static/11b699d88952ee57fbe4ffd5207d7451/b8331/ed.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"700px"}]},"width":700,"height":100}}},"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/ad998/ed.png 70w","sizes":"35px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/dbb7e/ed.webp 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/299bc/ed.webp 70w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"35px"}]},"width":35,"height":35}}}}}}},{"node":{"html":"<h1 id=\"variable-recovery\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#variable-recovery\" aria-label=\"variable recovery permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Variable Recovery</h1>\n<p>As far back as I can remember, one of the accepted dogmas of reverse engineering is that when a program is compiled, some information about the program is lost, and there is no way to recover it.  Variable names are one of the most frequently cited casualties of this idea.  In fact, this argument is used by countless authors in the introductions of their papers to explain some of the unique challenges that binary analysis has compared to source analysis.</p>\n<p>You can imagine how shocking (and cool!) it was then when my colleagues and I found that it's possible to recover a large percentage of variable names.  Our key insight is that the semantics of the binary code that accesses a variable is actually a surprisingly good signal for what the variable was named.  In other words, we took a huge amount of source code from github, compiled it, and then decompiled it.  We then trained a model to predict the variable names, which we can't see in an executable, based on the way that the code accesses those variables, which we can see in an executable.  In <i>Meaningful Variable Names for Decompiled Code: A Machine Translation Approach</i>, we showed that this was possible using Statistical Machine Translation, which is one of the techniques used to translate between natural languages.</p>\n<p>I'm happy to announce that our latest paper on this subject, <i>DIRE: A Neural Approach to Decompiled Identifier Renaming</i>, was accepted to ASE 2019.  In this paper, we found that neural network models work <i>really well</i> for recovering variable names in decompiled code.  I'll post our camera ready as soon as its finished.</p>\n<h1 id=\"code-reuse\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#code-reuse\" aria-label=\"code reuse permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Code Reuse</h1>\n<p>I'll be speaking at the 2019 <a href=\"https://cposc.org\">Central Pennsylvania Open Source Conference (CPOSC)</a> in September.  I attended CPOSC for the first time last year, and was very impressed by the quality of the talks.  The name is a little misleading; talks are not necessarily related to open source software.  I'll actually be giving a <a href=\"https://cposc.org/sessions/code-reuse-attacks-find/\">primer on code reuse attacks</a>.</p>","timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2019-08-17--august-2019-updates/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["publications","talks"],"title":"August 2019 Updates","updatedDate":"17 August, 2019","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/ad998/ed.png 70w","sizes":"35px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/dbb7e/ed.webp 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/299bc/ed.webp 70w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"35px"}]},"width":35,"height":35}}}}}}}]}},"pageContext":{"tag":"talks"}},"staticQueryHashes":[],"slicesMap":{}}